# Render Static Site routing (Netlify-style _redirects).
#
# IMPORTANT LIMITATION: Render's static-site _redirects parser does NOT
# reliably apply SPA-fallback rules like `/* /app.html 200` for paths
# that don't exist as real files. Deep links like /supplierManagement
# or /loginUni will return Render's own 404 page on reload.
#
# Workaround for users: deep-link via /app.html?route=/supplierManagement
# (which works as a direct-file access — the SPA loads with the route
# as a query param). The landing page's "Start Free Trial" and "Log in"
# buttons use this format for exactly this reason.
#
# This file is still deployed because the first rule below matches the
# real file /index.html (which exists) — that's the landing page.
# Future migration to Netlify/Vercel would enable full SPA fallback.
#
# build.sh copies this file into build/web/_redirects after flutter build.
/    /index.html   200
/*    /app.html   200
